 "why": "Near miss: Intro to Blender lesson 6 (\"The handle joins the mug in two places and the mesh is one piece\"). Extruding and bridging felt hard, so the learner added a Torus in Object mode (Shift+A > Mesh > Torus), scaled it to 0.35 and pushed it against the side of the mug. It looks like a handle in the viewport, but it is a second object: the Mug's own mesh is unchanged from lesson 5 (162 faces, one island) and the torus is its own island. Nothing joins them, so the mug and handle would come apart in any export.",
 "step": {
  "id": "s6",
  "index": 6,
  "title": "Build the handle",
  "file": "mug.blend",
  "instructions": "Select the mug and Tab into Edit mode. Pick the two faces on the side between your loop cuts, extrude them out (E), then join the two ends with Edge > Bridge Edge Loops so the handle meets the mug in two places. Tab out and save (Cmd+S).",
